{"record":"parent_entry","position":{"parent_record":"request:00000000000000000011:0000","subposition":null},"original_role":"tool","source":"tool_result","trust":"untrusted","provenance":null,"content":"{\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"call_id\":\"call_01a1894dc53a713188e8ff6039ebc410\",\"output\":\"Read text file `README.md`.\\n1|Hey, I'm Daniel, a dev by passion from near Frankfurt am Main, a hosting nerd and AI tinkerer, and currently in my second year of training as an IT specialist for system integration.\\n2|I live for technology, IT infrastructure and artificial intelligence, and learning by doing is my thing because I'd rather build servers than slide decks.\\n3|That AI tinkering includes ai-chat-webui, a privacy-focused chat UI for local Ollama models: https://github.com/drosemann/ai-chat-webui\\n4|I've been active in the Minecraft and hosting community for years, and since 22 April 2018 I've been running my Minecraft server ShadowUnity.\\n5|For my own projects I use my private stack, while at work I use the stack required there.\\n6|My full stack work covers HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Java, PHP, Python and React and TUI development.\\n7|My infrastructure work covers Docker, Linux, NGINX, Apache, Proxmox, Velocity and KVM with libvirt.\\n8|I have a lot of experience with the Pterodactyl and Coolify panels, but for my own services I now prefer pure Docker because it means less overhead and more control.\\n9|I have a lot of productive experience with MariaDB and I've tested Supabase extensively, both in the cloud and self hosted.\\n10|I use Cloudflare for DNS, HetrixTools for monitoring, Trello and Notion for project management for ShadowUnity, and Vercel for automatic deployments.\\n11|My browser survival game stranded-horizons is the one project still on Vercel auto-deploys: https://github.com/drosemann/stranded-horizons\\n12|On the client side I use Windows, with a nod to the games industry, and I plan to switch to Linux as soon as anticheat support gets better.\\n13|My focus is on cybersecurity, AI, cloud and virtualization, and automation with Python.\\n14|For that Python side I built aktienwerk, which turns SEC filings and stock prices for 100 US companies into plain explanations with only the standard library and SQLite: https://github.com/drosemann/aktienwerk\\n15|My hosting path went from Aternos to Ploudos to Minehub, which later closed.\\n16|After that it went through DeinServerHost, Strato, Host-Unlimited, LuxVPS and Mine-Hoster.\\n17|I cancelled ST-Hosting after one month because their LXC setup didn't meet my expectations, and HT-Hosting went insolvent, which taught me to migrate under time pressure.\\n18|I used Index Hosting until mid March and cancelled it because their AMD EPYC range was discontinued.\\n19|In between I tested Vercel and Kinsta, which had the best developer experience with edge and CDN, but self hosting is cheaper in the long run.\\n20|At times I ran three or four servers in parallel as development, failover and main systems.\\n21|Before my training I did three helpdesk internships, two school internships and one voluntary one, all unpaid and all just because I enjoyed the work.\\n22|I produced over 2,000 YouTube videos and streamed live for hundreds of hours, which taught me community building, live technology, video production, consistency and dealing with feedback.\\n23|ShadowUnity runs at play.shadowunity.de and hasn't had a reset since 2022.\\n24|Its plot system is streuland, my Paper plugin for protected vanilla-style plots instead of a standard grid: https://github.com/drosemann/streuland\\n25|Its name history is GrieferPrinz from the Pocket Edition days, inspired by GrieferKing and GrieferGames, then MelonenGames as my first Java server with only CityBuild, then DiamantSucht because that was my in game name, then DanielArmy during a personal brand phase, then MineRush, inspired by MineSucht by Abge and FloTastisch, and finally ShadowUnity, from ShadowFox plus community, which has been stable ever since.\\n26|From 24 January 2025 to 26 April 2025 I ran the DMH Network together with Matti and Henry.\\n27|Under my old alias MineHub I published SpigotMC plugins at https://www.spigotmc.org/resources/authors/minehub.1035036/\\n28|…","truncated":true}
